{
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "builtIn": 1,
        "datasource": {
          "type": "grafana",
          "uid": "-- Grafana --"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "hide": true,
        "iconColor": "rgba(0, 211, 255, 1)",
        "name": "Annotations & Alerts",
        "type": "dashboard"
      }
    ]
  },
  "description": "Scheduler policy analytics from the optional sacct textfile collector: queue waits, job outcomes, walltime accuracy and GPU-hours by account. The default range is 7 days on purpose - nothing here is an ops triage signal, and no rule in monitoring/rules/ alerts on any of it. In particular there is no job success-ratio SLO and no burn-rate paging: on a shared cluster most FAILED jobs are user error, and paging on them would page operators for mistakes they cannot fix. These panels answer policy questions - partition and QOS limits, walltime defaults, fairshare - on the timescale those decisions are actually made.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "links": [
    {
      "asDropdown": true,
      "icon": "external link",
      "includeVars": false,
      "keepTime": true,
      "tags": [
        "algalon"
      ],
      "targetBlank": false,
      "title": "Algalon dashboards",
      "tooltip": "Drill down into the fleet, queue and node views",
      "type": "dashboards",
      "url": ""
    }
  ],
  "panels": [
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Share of jobs that started within 30 minutes of submission, over 30 days. Recomputed from the raw histogram rather than averaged from the hourly algalon:sli:job_wait_ok_1h, so a busy afternoon weighs more than a quiet night. 0.90 is the target the threshold colours against - it is a policy number, tune it here.\n\nRequires the opt-in sacct textfile collector (monitoring/slurm/sacct-textfile.sh) on the slurmctld host; empty without it.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 3,
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.9
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percentunit"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "percentChangeColorMode": "standard",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.1.3",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(increase(slurm_job_wait_seconds_bucket{le=\"1800\"}[30d])) / sum(increase(slurm_job_wait_seconds_count[30d]))",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "started <30min",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Jobs started <30min (30d)",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "The wait a typical job actually experienced this week. Read it next to the tile on its left: a good median with a poor 30-day share means the pain is concentrated in a minority of jobs, which is a partition or QOS problem rather than a capacity one.\n\nRequires the opt-in sacct textfile collector (monitoring/slurm/sacct-textfile.sh) on the slurmctld host; empty without it.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 5,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "percentChangeColorMode": "standard",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.1.3",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le) (increase(slurm_job_wait_seconds_bucket[7d])))",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "median wait",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Median wait (7d)",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Fraction of finished jobs killed by the walltime limit. A rising share means the limit is set below what the work needs, and every timeout throws away all the compute the job had already done. This is a limit to raise, not a user to chase.\n\nRequires the opt-in sacct textfile collector (monitoring/slurm/sacct-textfile.sh) on the slurmctld host; empty without it.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 3,
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.02
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.05
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percentunit"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 10,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "percentChangeColorMode": "standard",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.1.3",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(increase(slurm_jobs_completed_total{state=\"timeout\"}[7d])) / sum(increase(slurm_jobs_completed_total[7d]))",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "timeout share",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Timeout share (7d)",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Allocated GPU-hours that finished this week: GPU count multiplied by runtime, summed over every terminal job. Allocated, not used - a job holding an idle GPU is counted here in full, which is exactly why SlurmJobGpuIdle exists alongside it.\n\nRequires the opt-in sacct textfile collector (monitoring/slurm/sacct-textfile.sh) on the slurmctld host; empty without it.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "none"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 15,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 4,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "percentChangeColorMode": "standard",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.1.3",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(increase(slurm_job_gpu_seconds_total[7d])) / 3600",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "GPU-hours",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "GPU-hours delivered (7d)",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Average fraction of time a GPU had a warp executing, over 7 days - the outcome measure for everything else on this page. GPU-hours by account says what the policy handed out; this says how much of it turned into computation.\n\nRead the two together in a QoS review: an account consuming a large share at a low effective utilization is a case for coaching or a smaller allocation, not for more hardware. Per-account effective hours are deliberately NOT computed - that needs per-job GPU attribution, which is only trustworthy on exclusive nodes (see the on(node) join limits in docs/slurm.md). Algalon does not publish a number it cannot stand behind.\n\nFull breakdown: Algalon / GPU Utilization Quality.\n\nRequires the DCGM_FI_PROF_* profiling fields in monitoring/exporters/dcgm-counters.csv (Volta or newer; conflicts with a concurrent Nsight/profiler session). Empty without them.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 3,
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.2
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.5
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percentunit"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 20,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 13,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "percentChangeColorMode": "standard",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.1.3",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "avg_over_time(avg(DCGM_FI_PROF_SM_ACTIVE)[7d:5m])",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "effective utilization",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Effective fleet utilization (7d)",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "p50 and p90 of time from submission to start, per partition. The gap between the two lines is the fairness question: a flat p50 under a climbing p90 means a few jobs are being starved by the partition's own limits while the median user sees nothing wrong.\n\nRequires the opt-in sacct textfile collector (monitoring/slurm/sacct-textfile.sh) on the slurmctld host; empty without it.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisBorderShow": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisColorMode": "text",
            "axisLabel": "wait",
            "axisPlacement": "left",
            "barAlignment": 0,
            "barWidthFactor": 0.6,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "hideFrom": {
              "legend": false,
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false
            },
            "insertNulls": false,
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "linear"
            },
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "none"
            },
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "off"
            }
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "id": 5,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "hideZeros": false,
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.1.3",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (partition, le) (rate(slurm_job_wait_seconds_bucket[1h])))",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "p50 {{partition}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.9, sum by (partition, le) (rate(slurm_job_wait_seconds_bucket[1h])))",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "p90 {{partition}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Queue wait quantiles by partition",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Pending jobs drawn over idle nodes. Pending with zero idle nodes is an honest capacity shortage and the queue is doing its job; pending *while* nodes sit idle is a scheduler policy fault - a partition, QOS, association or GRES constraint nothing can satisfy. SlurmQueueStalledWithIdleNodes alerts on the same pattern.\n\nComes from the live queue exporter, so this panel works without the sacct collector.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisBorderShow": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisColorMode": "text",
            "axisLabel": "count",
            "axisPlacement": "left",
            "barAlignment": 0,
            "barWidthFactor": 0.6,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "hideFrom": {
              "legend": false,
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false
            },
            "insertNulls": false,
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "linear"
            },
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "none"
            },
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "off"
            }
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "none",
          "min": 0,
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 4
      },
      "id": 6,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "hideZeros": false,
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.1.3",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "slurm_job_count_per_state{state=\"pending\"}",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "pending jobs",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "slurm_node_count_per_state{state=\"idle\"}",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "idle nodes",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Pending backlog vs idle nodes",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Jobs reaching each terminal state, stacked. Read it for shape, not for blame: a failure band that grows with the completed band is ordinary user attrition, while a failure band that spikes on its own is a cluster fault. Nothing here pages - most FAILED jobs are user error, and a success-ratio SLO would page operators for somebody else's typo.\n\nRequires the opt-in sacct textfile collector (monitoring/slurm/sacct-textfile.sh) on the slurmctld host; empty without it.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisBorderShow": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisColorMode": "text",
            "axisLabel": "jobs",
            "axisPlacement": "left",
            "barAlignment": 0,
            "barWidthFactor": 0.6,
            "drawStyle": "bars",
            "fillOpacity": 60,
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "hideFrom": {
              "legend": false,
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false
            },
            "insertNulls": false,
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "linear"
            },
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "normal"
            },
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "off"
            }
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "none",
          "min": 0,
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 12
      },
      "id": 7,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "hideZeros": false,
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.1.3",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (state) (increase(slurm_jobs_completed_total[1h]))",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "{{state}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Job outcomes per hour",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "How much of its requested walltime each job actually used, as a distribution over the last 7 days. Cumulative histogram buckets are subtracted pairwise here so each bar is a band, not a running total.\n\nMass at the low end is padded walltime: the scheduler cannot backfill a job into a gap it believes is too short, so over-requesting walltime leaves nodes idle in front of a full queue. Mass in 'over limit' is jobs the limit killed. Both ends are arguments for changing the partition's default and maximum time, not for talking to users one at a time.\n\nJobs submitted with UNLIMITED or a bare partition limit have no ratio and are absent from every band.\n\nRequires the opt-in sacct textfile collector (monitoring/slurm/sacct-textfile.sh) on the slurmctld host; empty without it.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "none"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 12
      },
      "id": 8,
      "options": {
        "displayMode": "lcd",
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": false
        },
        "maxVizHeight": 300,
        "minVizHeight": 16,
        "minVizWidth": 8,
        "namePlacement": "auto",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showUnfilled": true,
        "sizing": "auto",
        "valueMode": "color"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.1.3",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(increase(slurm_job_timelimit_used_ratio_bucket{le=\"0.1\"}[7d]))",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "0-10%",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(increase(slurm_job_timelimit_used_ratio_bucket{le=\"0.25\"}[7d])) - sum(increase(slurm_job_timelimit_used_ratio_bucket{le=\"0.1\"}[7d]))",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "10-25%",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(increase(slurm_job_timelimit_used_ratio_bucket{le=\"0.5\"}[7d])) - sum(increase(slurm_job_timelimit_used_ratio_bucket{le=\"0.25\"}[7d]))",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "25-50%",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "C"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(increase(slurm_job_timelimit_used_ratio_bucket{le=\"0.75\"}[7d])) - sum(increase(slurm_job_timelimit_used_ratio_bucket{le=\"0.5\"}[7d]))",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "50-75%",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "D"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
